@startuml
title Runtime ownership and deferred effects
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam defaultFontName SansSerif
skinparam defaultFontSize 14
skinparam ArrowColor #475569
skinparam componentBackgroundColor #EFF6FF
skinparam componentBorderColor #475569
skinparam packageBackgroundColor #F8FAFC
skinparam packageBorderColor #64748B
top to bottom direction
component "Worker threads\nControlHandle<C> clones" as workers
package "Runtime thread: cooperative execution" {
component "IoRuntime<C>\nMio Poll + Waker, bounded mailbox\nchecked resources and output queues" as runtime
component "Application A\nFSMs, schedulers, accounting\ncounters and protocol state" as app
component "DriverSet<A>\ntyped projections, static bounded entries\ncritical or optional failure policy" as drivers
component "RuntimeContext\nlogical snapshot + bounded FIFO effects\noutput quota and ticket reservations" as context
}
component "Registered std TCP/UDP sockets\nfrom std::net or optional net helpers" as sockets
workers --> runtime : typed commands + wake\nseparate shutdown latch
runtime --> workers : command processing receipts
sockets --> runtime : transfer ownership
runtime --> app : on_command / on_event / on_shutdown
runtime --> drivers : prepare / drive\nrelative clock hints and bounded quanta
drivers --> app : borrow component/context pairs
app --> context : record callback effects
drivers --> context : record driver effects
context --> runtime : commit FIFO after successful callback
note bottom of context
Successful send = admission, not completion.
Complete write = local kernel acceptance, not peer receipt.
Callback error/unwind cancels uncommitted effects;
application mutations are not rolled back.
end note
note left of drivers
Driver labels are not resource handles.
Component state is not owned by IoRuntime.
Callbacks and whole component batches cannot be preempted.
end note
@enduml
